{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner ruling on e0f5676d (R13 item 4: member read-token quota).\n\n1. Owner: one bucket per member, keyed by the authenticated membership ScopeRef and member identity, inside each destination object. Several keys of one member share the bucket. There is no global bucket and no bucket across incarnations.\n2. Cap: 8 open tokens per bucket, as proposed. Reserve the slot durably and atomically before the provider call.\n3. Open token: a slot is open from its reservation until the token's actual expiresAt. Taking or dropping the plaintext does not free it. An explicit minted:false frees it at once.\n4. Unknown mint (the provider reply is lost): the plaintext never reached dap or the caller, so nobody holds it. Count the slot as open until the reservation time plus the requested hours plus 10 minutes, then free it. No operator resolution step is needed. State in the docs that the quota counts reservations and is not proof that a provider token ended.\n5. Legacy: read markers with no member identity are not assigned to any bucket. They do not count, and they are not cleaned up by caller key or handle prefix. Same wording as the partial coverage accepted in 21a8e35b.\n6. The 1 to 24 hour request contract stays.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}